+++ b/src/workspace_app/kb/cards/prompts/card_synthesis.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+Below is everything a technical corpus states about one term, gathered from
+every document that mentioned it. Each line is a claim followed by the exact
+words from the document that make it.
+
+Write the term's card: one short definition that carries ALL of these claims and
+nothing else.
+
+TERM
+{term}
+
+STATEMENTS
+{statements}
+
+Two rules, and they are the whole task:
+
+- **Lose nothing.** Every claim above must be represented. Two claims about the
+  same term usually combine into one sentence rather than sitting side by side —
+  "is a fruit" and "is red" become "a red fruit", not "It is a fruit. It is
+  red."
+- **Add nothing.** Do not draw on anything you know about this term from outside
+  the statements above, however obvious it seems. What the corpus did not say is
+  not part of this card; a reader who wanted general knowledge would not be
+  looking here.
+
+Write 1–3 sentences. State what the thing IS, not where it appeared. Use the
+corpus's own vocabulary — if the statements say 回焊爐, the card says 回焊爐.
+
+Output ONLY a JSON object of this exact shape — no prose, no code fence:
+
+{"title": "...", "body": "..."}
